From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Austin Schuh <austin.linux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:50:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Use vsnprintf in buffer_appendf

macOS deprecates vsprintf, which fails builds without _FORTIFY_SOURCE,
such as ASan ones, under -Werror. The buffer is already sized for the
output, so vsnprintf with that size writes the same thing.
---
 common/string_util.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/string_util.c b/common/string_util.c
index f7da2b8d77960febe07c52f770a9c4e3bbda29f0..7d71629ca233c0af52a8c4f058f72fdf0f51384a 100644
--- a/common/string_util.c
+++ b/common/string_util.c
@@ -700,7 +700,7 @@ static void buffer_appendf(char **_buf, int *bufpos, void *fmt, ...)
     if (slen >= salloc) {
         s = realloc(s, slen + 1);
         va_start(ap, fmt);
-        vsprintf((char*) s, fmt, ap);
+        vsnprintf(s, slen + 1, fmt, ap);
         va_end(ap);
     }
 
